#d	Khmer words by English word, machine-made by word-aligning 7 Khmer Bibles with 8 English ones, and Khmer–English sentence pairs from <a href="https://opus.nlpl.eu/">OPUS</a> (subtitles, web pages, KDE and translatewiki software strings, Wikipedia names and pages, TICO-19, Global Voices, TED talks, Tatoeba, NLLB) and FLORES-200, with eflomal: an English word’s commonest Khmer, commonest first, by sense (English Wiktionary’s, CC BY-SA, and Open English WordNet’s; told apart by the sentences, the other languages’ Bibles and ALT, and the Bible’s Greek and Hebrew), with an example sentence from openly licensed sources (CC BY, CC BY-SA, public domain). People’s translations first, and added where the aligner missed them: English Wiktionary’s translation tables (by sense), the English glosses of Wiktionary’s Khmer entries (via Kaikki) and the SBBIC English–Khmer dictionary’s (GPL 2); a machine-aligned Khmer word only where one of these gives it, or a Khmer dictionary has it (Headley’s and Chuon Nath’s, only to check by), or a good share of the sentences do. With another language’s on, a dictionary between them. (Archaic): English only the KJV and ASV have; a corpus’s name after a word only it has. Unchecked: verify before relying on it.
